  Device (vendor) VINTF manifest for the X-ROM x1 reference board.

  Intentionally empty in Session 1.

  target-level is the Framework Compatibility Matrix version this vendor image
  is built against: 8 for Android 14, 202404 for Android 15, 202504 for
  Android 16. Raise it when the board is rebased, and run the VTS Treble suites
  afterwards — a target-level that does not match the framework is what makes a
  GSI refuse to boot on this vendor image.

  Nothing AVF-related belongs here. android.system.virtualizationservice is a
  platform service registered with servicemanager and labelled in
  service_contexts; it is not a vendor HAL and it is not part of VINTF.
  Likewise android.xrom.isolation.IXIsolationService is a platform-internal
  service in system_ext, consumed only by other system_ext code on the same
  side of the Treble boundary. VINTF governs the vendor/framework contract, so
  neither service is declared here.
-->
<manifest version="1.0" type="device" target-level="8">
</manifest>
